I've written the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The files are on disk, and I assume the harness reads them from there.

Task 1 — Fixes #1091 (search, product). Today yoyo grep hello a b joins the two paths into one and searches a b. The task makes grep take several paths, which is what grep -r and git grep both do.
• Tests first, in a new sibling test file. Each input the old joining treated alike gets its own case: no path, one path, two paths, one path with a space in its name (this must still be searched as one path), and a second path that doesn't exist.
• Both kinds of directory: each case runs in a plain folder and in a git repo, which also covers the git-grep branch the ticket says nobody has checked yet.
• Size limit: commands_search.rs is already over its line limit, so the task keeps new code in it to a minimum.
• Why this one: it's outside the prompt code, which got 5 of the last 10 changes.

Task 2 — Part of #1012 (cost, product, using the slot for clearing the oldest open issue). This is the next step the Day 241 reflection comment on #1012 asked for.
• The fact: xAI's pricing and regions pages say the 10% extra charge applies only to requests sent to the US endpoint, us.api.x.ai. yoyo picks the endpoint itself, so it can tell which price applies.
• Already checked: the resolved base_url is available in cli.rs (around line 1084), next to the existing pricing setter (around line 2471).
• The change: grok-4.6 drops back to the base rate on the default endpoint. grok-4.6 and grok-4.7 get the 10% extra only on the US endpoint. A price the user set in their own config still wins.
• Effect: grok-4.7 comes off the docs' list of prices that read low.
• Safeguards: the task first re-reads xAI's page and stops if the page says something different. New logic goes in a new module, because cost.rs is at its line limit.

